        "position": 6,
        "title": "Good comb, requires careful brushing",
        "text": "I like this comb and use both sides. Comb the dog to ensure all tangles are gone. And have learned to lay it pretty flat and hold the skin a bit. Really carefully then running the coarse comb flat over the skin and through the coat. I've hit myself and bleed almost every time if I'm not careful... so it's one of those. If you use it right... no issues here.The flea side works well and is sturdy. It is fine and does require a smooth coat. Some days I brush out a dozen or two ticks of all ages/sizes easily. But you do have to make sure your dog is well groomed.Otherwise, I wouldn't use this brushIt's just not pleasant for the animal that way. Unlike others, zero issues with the teeth. I used this (both sides) daily for monthNo issues.",
